stion/worked-solution "For any linear differential operator,\n\n$$\nL(a{y}_{1}(x)+b{y}_{2}(x))=aL({y}_{1}(x))+bL({y}_{2}(x))\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(2{y}_{1}-{y}_{2}) & =2L({y}_{1})-L({y}_{2}) \\\\  & =2({e}^{x}+1)-(2{e}^{x}-3) \\\\  & =2{e}^{x}+2-2{e}^{x}+3 \\\\  & =(2{e}^{x}-2{e}^{x})+(2+3) \\\\  & =0+5 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-130077/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "68148c93-9139-5deb-8a53-a05d63ec5930"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130077"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
